\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The race that long in darkness pined
\par Has seen a glorious Light;
\par The people dwell in day, who dwelt
\par In death's surrounding night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. To hail Thy rise, Thou better Sun,
\par The gathering nations come,
\par Joyous as when the reapers bear
\par The harvest-treasures home.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To us Child of Hope is born,
\par To us a Son is given;
\par Him shall the tribes of earth obey,
\par Him all the hosts of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. His name shall be the Prince of Peace,
\par For evermore adored,
\par The Wonderful, the Counsellor,
\par The great and might Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. His power increasing still shall spread,
\par His reign no end shall know;
\par Justice shall guard His throne above,
\par And peace abound below.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

